(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase470RestoreGateScopeAndReachExecution"
  :createdAt 1789310000000
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 1
  :summary "Restore Gate Scope and Reach Execution: make a green gate mean a green corpus again, close the seven remaining module names, reconcile the installed binary with the built one, and clear the path to tasks that can actually be claimed."
  :phase "Phase470RestoreGateScopeAndReachExecution"
  :baseline "Audited 2026-09-12 and recorded in D81ExecutionAudit20260912. Failing suites fell from 142 to 46 of 314 and distinct unresolved modules from 36 to 7; errors are now located, ERR_TEST_RESULT_NOT_TRUE exists for the first time, nine acceptance fixtures execute 133 assertions and Task43601 passes its full gate. In the same window gate 5 narrowed: asl.c:2662 invokes the runner as bash run-gate-tests.sh bin/asl node asl/packages/asl-gates/tests and collects assertions only from that directory, auditing 5 suites and reporting 171 assertions, so asl audit gates prints all seven gates passed while 46 suites fail. Run against the whole tree the same runner exits 1 with 45 failures, so the runner is correct and the scope handed to it is not. Separately the asl on PATH has digest 6be341c3 while the repository binary has 947ab120, and nothing reports the divergence."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task47001" :parentId "" :phase "phase-470"
      :title "Gate 5 audits the corpus, not a directory"
      :kind :engine :state :planned :lane "scope" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789310000000 :updatedAt 1789310000000
      :motivation "A gate that passes because it narrowed its scope is indistinguishable from a gate that passes because the system is correct, and the difference here is 46 failing suites. The runner was repaired and then strengthened, and the repair was bypassed one level up by handing it five suites instead of the tree. Every acceptance gate runs asl audit gates as its second step, so every task certified from now until this is fixed is certified against five suites."
      :purpose "Gate 5 runs the runner over the whole workspace and counts what the runner executed. A deliberately reduced scope is permitted only when it is declared in the output, so a narrowed run says it was narrowed and by how much, and cannot be mistaken for a full one."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Gate 5 covering the corpus" "A narrowed scope declared in the output" "A green gate meaning a green corpus" "The 46 failures visible where they belong"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_5_suites" "collect_tree_files"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "output" "grading"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47001"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47001.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["With a failing suite anywhere in the tree, gate 5 fails." "The suite count gate 5 reports equals the count the runner executed." "A narrowed scope appears in the output, so it cannot be silent."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47001" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Restore the workspace scope." "Report the scope in the output." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task47002" :parentId "" :phase "phase-470"
      :title "Close the seven remaining module names"
      :kind :remediation :state :planned :lane "binding" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789310000000 :updatedAt 1789310000000
      :motivation "What was 36 unresolved names across 113 suites is now 7: posts, core/process, mem/src/xref, examples/blink, daemon, a compiler path used as a module name, and api/packages. This is no longer an architectural problem, it is a list. One of them is daemon, which is an import of a subsystem this programme retired into the engine."
      :purpose "Each of the seven is resolved, repointed or removed, with the decision recorded per name. An import of a retired subsystem is removed rather than satisfied. A path used where a module name belongs is corrected."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Seven names closed with a recorded decision each" "The retired daemon no longer imported" "Paths no longer used as module names"]
      :owns ["agent/src" "mem/src" "intel/src" "asl/packages" "asl-arduino"]
      :targetSymbols ["daemon"] :relatedSymbols ["semantics" "foreign"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47001"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47002"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47002.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["No import in the corpus names a module that resolves nowhere." "An import of a retired subsystem fails the check even if a file of that name is later added." "A module name containing a path separator that is a path rather than a module name is reported."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47002" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Decide each of the seven." "Remove retired imports." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task47003" :parentId "" :phase "phase-470"
      :title "The installed binary is the built binary"
      :kind :tooling :state :planned :lane "build" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789310000000 :updatedAt 1789310000000
      :motivation "The asl an agent runs has digest 6be341c3 and the one the repository builds has 947ab120. Every measurement taken by following the instructions describes a program the repository does not contain, and every gate the repository runs describes a program the agent does not use. Neither side can detect the difference today."
      :purpose "The installed binary reports the digest of the source it was built from, and a command run against a workspace whose build differs says so before doing anything else. Reconciling is a single step and is not silent."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["The binary reports its source digest" "A divergence is announced, not discovered" "Measurements and gates refer to one program"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "scripts/build_and_install.sh" "scripts/install.sh"]
      :targetSymbols ["main"] :relatedSymbols ["capabilities" "gates" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47003"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47003.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A binary built from a different source than the workspace is detected on the first command." "The reported digest changes when the source changes." "A matching pair produces no warning, so the check is not noise."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47003" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Embed the source digest." "Compare on invocation." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task47004" :parentId "" :phase "phase-470"
      :title "Fixtures for the tasks that are ready, so work can be claimed"
      :kind :verification :state :planned :lane "execution" :priority :critical :ownerRole "verifier"
      :createdAt 1789310000000 :updatedAt 1789310000000
      :motivation "Nine fixtures exist against roughly one hundred and eighty tasks, and a task without one exits 3 at its own gate. The programme is fully specified and mostly unclaimable, and the missing artefact is the one the ownership contract says its author may not write."
      :purpose "Every task with no blocking dependency has a fixture written by its verifier before the work begins, composed by the doctrine: the negative case first, inversion producing a non zero exit, and a stub returning a constant failing at least one case. Fixture coverage for the ready set reaches complete, so the ready set is genuinely ready."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A fixture for every dependency-free task" "Written by the verifier, before the work" "Inversion checked on each" "The ready set becomes claimable"]
      :owns ["tests/acceptance/d81"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "grading" "hiddenTests"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47001"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47004"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47004.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Every dependency-free task has a fixture whose inversion fails." "A fixture passing against a constant-returning stub is reported." "A task claimed without a fixture is refused."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47004" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Enumerate the ready set." "Write fixtures by verifier." "Check inversion." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task47005" :parentId "" :phase "phase-470"
      :title "A gate cannot narrow its own scope without saying so"
      :kind :verification :state :planned :lane "scope" :priority :critical :ownerRole "verifier"
      :createdAt 1789310000000 :updatedAt 1789310000000
      :motivation "Three distinct gates in this programme have passed while the condition they described was false, and the newest one did it by a mechanism none of the earlier fixes anticipated: it kept working correctly and was given less to look at. Fixing instances one at a time has not held, because the family is larger than any instance."
      :purpose "Every gate reports the extent of what it examined alongside its verdict, and the extent is compared against the extent of the thing it claims to cover. A gate whose coverage falls without a declared reason fails, so narrowing becomes as visible as failing."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Coverage reported beside every verdict" "A silent narrowing fails" "The family closed rather than the instance"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "tests/acceptance/d81"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_5_suites" "run_gate_6_grammar" "run_gate_7_skills"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "output" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47001" "Task45506"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47005"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47005.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Reducing a gate's scope without declaring it fails the run." "Coverage is recomputed each run rather than recorded." "A declared reduction passes and appears in the output."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47005" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Report coverage per gate." "Compare against the claimed extent." "Fail silent narrowing." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 0 :receipts [])]
  :notes "Task47001 is the single change that restores meaning to every acceptance gate below it, and it has no dependencies. Task47005 exists because this is the third distinct mechanism by which a gate in this repository has reported success while the condition was false.")
